conflict {R8, R12, R14}
R8, R12, and R14 cannot all hold.

R8 line 32
When the customer is subscribing and the customer is not cancelling and the customer is signed in, the Checkout shall start the subscription.

R12 line 36
When the subscription is started, the Checkout shall route the order to the fulfill lane.

R14 line 38
When the customer is subscribing, the Checkout shall route the order to the hold lane.

They clash when the cart was not open, an item was not added, checkout was not started, payment was not submitted, payment was not declined, the address was not confirmed, the customer was subscribing, the customer was not cancelling, the customer was signed in, a card was not saved, and stock was not available.
R8 requires that the subscription was started.
R14 requires that the order was routed to the hold lane.

Example scenario:
{
  "cart_opened": false,
  "item_added": false,
  "checkout_started": false,
  "payment_submitted": false,
  "payment_declined": false,
  "address_confirmed": false,
  "subscribe_clicked": true,
  "cancel_requested": false,
  "signed_in": true,
  "card_saved": false,
  "stock_ok": false,
  "order_accepted": false,
  "order_rejected": false,
  "subscription_started": true,
  "receipt_sent": false,
  "lane": "fulfill",
  "billed_seats": 1
}
This scenario keeps R8 and R12 and breaks R14.

Suggested fix: ask which requirement should win. Removing any one of R8, R12, and R14 leaves the rest consistent.

Candidate repairs follow. This report does not choose one.

repair drop R8
One repair is to drop R8 and keep R12 and R14 as written.
When the subscription is started, the Checkout shall route the order to the fulfill lane.
When the customer is subscribing, the Checkout shall route the order to the hold lane.

repair drop R12
One repair is to drop R12 and keep R8 and R14 as written.
When the customer is subscribing and the customer is not cancelling and the customer is signed in, the Checkout shall start the subscription.
When the customer is subscribing, the Checkout shall route the order to the hold lane.

repair drop R14
One repair is to drop R14 and keep R8 and R12 as written.
When the customer is subscribing and the customer is not cancelling and the customer is signed in, the Checkout shall start the subscription.
When the subscription is started, the Checkout shall route the order to the fulfill lane.

repair strengthen R12
One repair is to add "and the customer is not subscribing" to the condition of R12. R8 and R14 stay as written.
When the subscription is started and the customer is not subscribing, the Checkout shall route the order to the fulfill lane.

repair strengthen R12
One repair is to add "and the customer is cancelling" to the condition of R12. R8 and R14 stay as written.
When the subscription is started and the customer is cancelling, the Checkout shall route the order to the fulfill lane.

repair strengthen R12
One repair is to add "and the customer is not signed in" to the condition of R12. R8 and R14 stay as written.
When the subscription is started and the customer is not signed in, the Checkout shall route the order to the fulfill lane.

repair strengthen R14
One repair is to add "and the customer is cancelling" to the condition of R14. R8 and R12 stay as written.
When the customer is subscribing and the customer is cancelling, the Checkout shall route the order to the hold lane.

repair strengthen R14
One repair is to add "and the customer is not signed in" to the condition of R14. R8 and R12 stay as written.
When the customer is subscribing and the customer is not signed in, the Checkout shall route the order to the hold lane.

